# Copy to `.env` in this directory. `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` vars are inlined into the
# bundle by Expo — never put a secret here; this file is for addresses and
# public keys only.

# Where the API is. `localhost` is always wrong on a physical device: the phone
# resolves it to itself. Use the dev machine's LAN address, the one `expo start`
# prints in the QR URL.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.5:5000

# Razorpay's PUBLIC key id (`rzp_test_…` / `rzp_live_…`). Safe in a bundle by
# design — the secret and the webhook secret live on the server and never here.
#
# ✅ The client's account exists and the keys landed 2026-08-08, so the server is
# live. Unset here, the app offers **cash on delivery only**.
#
# ⚠️ **Setting it in this file is not enough for a built APK, and that is the
# trap.** `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` is inlined by Expo at BUNDLE time, and `*.env` is in
# `.gitignore` while EAS uploads only what git tracks — so an `eas build` never
# sees this file, bakes in "no key", and the APK offers cash only however many
# times you edit it here. Two different fixes for two different situations:
#
#   • Dev client + local Metro — this file IS read, but Metro caches the
#     transform. Restart with `npx expo start --clear`, then reload the app.
#   • Any `eas build` (development / preview / production) — the value has to
#     reach the builder, not your disk:
#         eas env:create --name EXPO_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID \
#           --value rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx --visibility plaintext \
#           --environment development --environment preview
#     "plaintext" is correct here and not a slip: this key id ships inside every
#     APK by design. The SECRET is a server variable and must never be an
#     `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` anything.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=

# Reminders, not settings — both are separate processes and this app is nearly
# useless without them running against the same API:
#
#   npm run server      the API itself.
#   npm run sweeper     enforces the 60-second accept window. Without it an
#                       order placed here sits at ROUTING forever: no offer ever
#                       expires, no shop is ever asked twice, and nothing
#                       reaches a rider. The tracking screen will show "finding
#                       you a shop" until the end of time.
